    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The seam with the window you just learned comes first. The E form's window ends at fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and this one starts at fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "6",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", so frets "
        },
        {
          "text": "6–8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " belong to both. Six dots live there — "
        },
        {
          "text": "6·8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "b7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "1·8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — one on every string, all five notes of the scale between them. Every one of those six is a dot the fret-5 box already handed you, because the E form's window reaches all the way to fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". That is the point rather than a disappointment: the overlap is not a new shape, it is the top of the box you were already standing in. What is genuinely new starts at fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "9",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "'s row is the hinge — "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". It belongs to both windows at once, and "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is a root in both — one of the E form's three, one of this window's two. Keep a finger on it and your hand can travel two frets up the neck without the scale changing underneath it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "tip",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "4·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is a root in both windows at once. It is the note to hold on to while your hand moves from one to the other."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There's a second seam above it. Frets "
        },
        {
          "text": "9–10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " belong to this window and to the C form's at once, and hold six more dots — "
        },
        {
          "text": "6·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "b7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·9",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "1·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — again one per string, again all five notes. This window has a doorway at each end, which is exactly what makes it the bridge."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seven of the twelve dots are "
        },
        {
          "text": "Am",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ": "
        },
        {
          "text": "6·8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·9",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "1·8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Five aren't: "
        },
        {
          "text": "6·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "1·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Its character is in where the roots sit. Both — "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — are on inside strings; there's no root on string 6 or string 1 anywhere in this window. Combined with three "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "s and three "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "s, that means the outside of the hand never lands home here: strings 6 and 1 each offer a "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and a "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and nothing else. That's why this window feels unfinished on its own, and why it works best as a passage between the two either side of it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In reach it's compact: its three-fret strings are 5 and 4, right in the middle of the hand, and its dots sit on four consecutive frets — "
        },
        {
          "text": "7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "9",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — with none of them skipped. Only the open-position window manages that too. The C form leaves fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "11",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " empty, the G form leaves fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", and the fret-5 box uses only three frets of the four it spans."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Play from "
        },
        {
          "text": "6·5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " in the fret-5 box up to "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " in this window without stopping, and notice that the only thing that happened was your hand moving two frets. Page from one window to the next in the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Scale Visualizer",
          "link": {
            "kind": "screen",
            "href": "/scale-visualizer"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and watch the overlap for yourself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That's five windows done. One question is left: what the app's other toggle is showing when it calls the same dots something else."
        }
      ]
    },
